  "details": "Multiplayer synchronization issue with VRCStation-based animations on standalone Meta Quest headsets.\n\nWhen multiple players participate, each player can see their own avatar performing the assigned animation correctly. However, other players cannot see that avatar performing. Instead, the remote avatar appears standing still at its original starting position, even though the player is actively performing on their own headset.\n\n[You can see this in the MMD Dance Worlds, for example.]\n\nIt appears to be working fine on PC and that it is only affecting Quest headset users.\n\nI've also noticed existing reports of station synchronization issues, and this behavior appears similar.\n\nThank you for looking into this. Any assistance would be greatly appreciated.",
